The code statements that lead to the bug are:
put_attrs_out:
	kobject_put(&context->attrs->kobj);
	context->attrs = NULL;
	return err;
Reason:
When `damon_sysfs_context_add_dirs()` fails after `damon_sysfs_attrs_add_dirs()` has created subdirectories under `attrs/`, the error path merely drops the `attrs` kobject reference without first removing those subdirectories. This leaves orphaned sysfs entries, corrupting the interface and leaking memory.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
rmdir_put_attrs_out:
	damon_sysfs_attrs_rm_dirs(context->attrs);
	kobject_put(&context->attrs->kobj);
	context->attrs = NULL;
	return err;
Reason:
By adding a call to `damon_sysfs_attrs_rm_dirs()` before the `kobject_put()`, the fix ensures that any `attrs/` subdirectories created before the failure are properly cleaned up. This restores sysfs integrity and prevents memory leaks.

